<title>USA: Charleston, W.Va., approves $5.2 million GOs.</title>
<headline>Charleston, W.Va., approves $5.2 million GOs.</headline>
<dateline>CHARLESTON, W.Va. 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Charleston, W. Va., City Council has approved a $5.2 million general obligation bond issue for parks and public safety projects, the Post and Courier reported Wednesday.</p>
<p>The proposal passed 12-1 at a council meeting Tuesday and would raise property taxes by about $6 a year on a $100,000 home.</p>
<p>Voter approval is not required because of the small size of the issue.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
